description: Runtime permission handling for telephony APIs — checks, graceful denial, and UI fallback
alwaysApply: true
---

# Permissions

## Mandatory Runtime Checks

- Every single call to `TelephonyManager`, `TelephonyCallback`, or any
  `CellInfo` API MUST be preceded by a strict runtime permission check for
  BOTH `ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION` and `READ_PHONE_STATE`.
- Check both permissions explicitly (e.g.
  `ContextCompat.checkSelfPermission(...) == PackageManager.PERMISSION_GRANTED`
  for each) immediately before the call site — do not assume a manifest
  declaration or an earlier check elsewhere is sufficient.

## No Crashes on Denial

- Permission denial MUST NOT cause a crash (no uncaught `SecurityException`).
- On denial, the data/telephony layer must emit an explicit empty or error
  state upward — never `null`, an exception, or silent no-op.
- The ViewModel must surface this as an explicit state, e.g.
  `PermissionsRequiredState`, as part of its `StateFlow`/UI state — not as a
  side effect, log line, or toast alone.

## UI Fallback

- The Compose UI must observe this state and, when active, render a
  fallback "Permissions Required" screen with a rationale explaining why
  `ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION` and `READ_PHONE_STATE` are needed, instead of the
  main dashboard.
- The main dashboard/content Composable must never be rendered while
  permissions are missing.
